{% comment %} Staleness. `as_of_epoch` is when the laptop last pushed; `"now"`
is whenever TRMNL last rendered this markup. The gap between them is how old
the numbers on the glass actually are.

90 minutes because this screen pushes hourly — past that, a scheduled push was
missed outright, which in practice means the laptop was suspended. Normal
cadence jitter never trips it.

In practice this branch is unreachable: TRMNL skips screen generation when the
merge variables have not changed, and a webhook plugin's variables change only
when we push. No push, no render, so `now_s` is frozen at the last render and
`age_m` stays ~0. Kept anyway — it costs ~20 bytes and is correct if TRMNL ever
renders on a wall clock. The line doing the real work is `as_of` in the title
bar, stamped at push time. See CLAUDE.md, "The quiet version of that failure".
{% endcomment %}
{% assign now_s = "now" | date: "%s" | plus: 0 %}
{% assign age_m = now_s | minus: as_of_epoch | divided_by: 60 | floor %}
{% if age_m >= 90 %}{% assign stale = true %}{% else %}{% assign stale = false %}{% endif %}

<div class="layout layout--top">
  {% if active == 1 %}
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="col--span-5">
        {% comment %} value--xxlarge, not mega: at mega "17:00" is wider than a
        5-column cell and overruns into the model list beside it. Grid cells do
        not clip, so an oversized value silently overlaps its neighbour.
        flex--left keeps this column's alignment matching the one beside it. {% endcomment %}
        <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap">
          <span class="label label--underline">Resets at</span>
          {% comment %} resets_at is an absolute clock time — it does not move
          within a block, so it stays honest however old this render is.
          Everything under it is computed against collection time and decays,
          which is why the guard wraps those lines and not this one. {% endcomment %}
          <span class="value value--xxlarge value--tnums">{{ resets_at }}</span>
          {% unless stale %}
            <span class="label">{{ left_approx }} left</span>
            <span class="label label--gray">{{ block_tokens }} this block · {{ burn_per_min }}/min</span>
          {% else %}
            {% comment %} An hours-old "about 3h 30m left" is not stale, it is
            wrong, and burn_per_min divides by an elapsed time that kept growing
            after the push. block_tokens survives the cut: it undercounts rather
            than lying, and saying so out loud is the whole point of the screen. {% endcomment %}
            <span class="label label--gray">{{ block_tokens }} as of {{ as_of }}</span>
            <span class="label label--gray">laptop asleep — not live</span>
          {% endunless %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col--span-7">
        <div class="flex flex--col flex--left">
          <span class="label label--underline">Today — {{ day_tokens }}</span>
          {% for m in models %}
            <div class="item">
              <div class="content">
                <span class="title title--base">{{ m.n }}</span>
                <span class="description description--small">{{ m.t }} · {{ m.p }}% of today</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
          {% comment %} "Currently" is a claim about right now, so it goes with
          the other decaying lines. The model split above it is a snapshot of a
          finished day and reads fine at any age. {% endcomment %}
          {% if top_model != "" and stale == false %}
            <span class="label label--gray">Currently mostly {{ top_model }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {% else %}
    {% comment %} No open block. Not an error — nothing sent for five hours, so
    the day's total is the useful thing to say, not a zero. {% endcomment %}
    <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap">
      <span class="value value--xlarge">No active block</span>
      <span class="label label--gray">{{ day_tokens }} used today</span>
      {% for m in models %}
        <div class="item">
          <div class="content">
            <span class="title title--base">{{ m.n }}</span>
            <span class="description description--small">{{ m.t }} · {{ m.p }}%</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  <span class="title">Claude usage</span>
  {% comment %} "as of" rather than a bare clock: the old markup put "21:19"
  here, which at a glance reads as the current time instead of as the age of
  what is on screen. {% endcomment %}
  <span class="instance">as of {{ as_of }}{% if stale %} · {% if age_m < 120 %}{{ age_m }}m{% else %}{{ age_m | divided_by: 60 | floor }}h{% endif %} old{% endif %}</span>
</div>
